{
    "article_summary": "The article describes an aryl radical-mediated NHC organocatalysis method. By utilizing the enolate form of the Breslow intermediate as a single electron donor, aryl radicals are generated from aryl iodides via a thermodynamically unfavored but kinetically feasible SET process. These radicals are then applied to radical relay-type arylacylation of styrenes and \u03b1-amino C(sp3)-H acylation of secondary amides, eliminating the need for metals, light, or external oxidants/reductants.",
